HOW THE PROJECT READS IT (an engineering reading, not legal advice)

A bundle is data. A program that reads a bundle as its input, as the Sixkey extension does, is not thereby a work based
on the rules: the extension keeps its own licence, and so does any other program that reads the same format. Copying,
changing or passing on the rules or a bundle is what this licence governs. If you give a changed bundle to others, in a
build or as a download, give them the changed rule files, fixtures and tools as well, under AGPL-3.0-or-later, and say in
the bundle's "source" field where they are.

WHERE THE SOURCE IS

Each bundle names its source in its "source" field: the repository at the tag rules-v<version>, where <version> is the
bundle's own. A bundle built before the repository had a public address has an empty "source"; such a bundle is not
for distribution in a store package.

